WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:01.901
[dramatic music]

00:00:01.967 --> 00:00:03.403
 Bladesmiths, congratulations.

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:04.938
You've made it to the final
round of this competition.

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:06.372
Now it's time for you
to go back to your home

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:09.009
forges and recreate this
iconic weapon from history--

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:14.113
a Bhuj.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.214
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:16.382
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:17.183
 [inaudible].

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.517 line:7%
 Good luck to you, buddy.

00:00:18.617 --> 00:00:20.153 line:7%
[rock music]

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:21.354
BENTON: So it's day one.

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:22.922
I'm back home in
Evansville, Indiana,

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:24.624
and I'm ready to get
started on this Bhuj build.

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.495
I'm working on the dagger first.

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:34.133
I think it's the easiest thing
to warm up and start with.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.235
I really got to
watch my dimensions.

00:00:36.335 --> 00:00:37.770
This dagger, as
I'm forging it, I'm

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:40.306
keeping in mind that where
the ricasso and the transition

00:00:40.372 --> 00:00:42.241
from the blade to
the tang is, I got

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:45.011
to make sure I'm
not too wide to go

00:00:45.077 --> 00:00:46.980
inside the handle and the pipe.

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:48.347
I got to make sure
I'm not too narrow

00:00:48.447 --> 00:00:50.050
or this thing's going
to rattle around.

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:52.718
So I really have a tight
window that I need to fit in.

00:00:52.785 --> 00:00:54.421
Good enough for now.

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:57.457
I made some great progress,
but I've got a lot to do.

00:00:57.557 --> 00:01:00.693 line:7%
It's freaking me out.

00:01:00.759 --> 00:01:01.661
JOE: It's day one.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:03.095
I'm here at the home forge.

00:01:03.162 --> 00:01:04.831
Get warm in here,
man-- it's freezing.

00:01:04.897 --> 00:01:06.665
I'm making a Bhuj.

00:01:06.765 --> 00:01:10.336
It's a little bit boujie, I
would say-- a little bourgeois.

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:13.105
It's not only a
piece for warfare,

00:01:13.172 --> 00:01:15.107
but it's a really
artistic expression

00:01:15.174 --> 00:01:17.410
of whoever's carrying it.

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.279 line:0%
I'm thinking of
doing some san mai,

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:21.547 line:0%
so sandwiching it
with a mild steel.

00:01:21.647 --> 00:01:25.217 line:0%
That'll just make it
that much more tough.

00:01:25.284 --> 00:01:28.187
I chose san mai to really
bring the most out of these two

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:29.389
different types of steels.

00:01:29.455 --> 00:01:30.990
The mild steel is very tough.

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:33.226
It can take a lot of
bending without cracking,

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:35.728
while the hardened
51/60 in the center

00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:38.865
is just coming down where
I need it along the edge.

00:01:38.931 --> 00:01:42.969
Just need to get the billet
down to a more manageable size.

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:44.637
I hot cut off the excess.

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:47.639
And as I'm hot cutting, I'm
putting a lot of stresses

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.308
on those welds.

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:51.677
And one of the pieces of mild
steel's wanting to kind of rip

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:52.811
away.

00:01:52.878 --> 00:01:54.347
That's pretty bad news.

00:01:54.413 --> 00:01:57.150
From hot cutting it,
all the stresses on it

00:01:57.216 --> 00:01:59.252
found a weak point right there.

00:01:59.318 --> 00:02:01.387
So in order to fix
that delamination,

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:03.922
I got a few more tries at forge
welding it up to the thickness

00:02:03.989 --> 00:02:05.157
that I have.

00:02:05.257 --> 00:02:08.060
If I get too thin,
then it's a lost cause.

00:02:08.127 --> 00:02:11.364 line:0%
I just hope I can
make this work.

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:16.102 line:0%
 Not only is it day two, but
it is also my 28th birthday.

00:02:16.168 --> 00:02:18.437
Creating a challenge
weapon in my home shop,

00:02:18.504 --> 00:02:20.139
that's a pretty cool
birthday present.

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:21.407
Today, I'm going
to start forging

00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:23.676
the larger blade of the Bhuj.

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:27.413
So what I'm trying to do is
split this tang off of here,

00:02:27.513 --> 00:02:30.749
and I got to form my clip point.

00:02:30.849 --> 00:02:34.287
Then I can draw my length out,
and that shape will follow.

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:36.255
And then I can start
getting that swoop

00:02:36.321 --> 00:02:39.458
that I need for that Bhuj look.

00:02:39.559 --> 00:02:41.394
Time to get this
bad boy quenched.

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:44.296
This is the moment that
I really need to nail,

00:02:44.363 --> 00:02:47.934
and I am praying that this
thing's going to stay straight.

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:49.535
I pull it out.

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:51.838
[laughing]

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:55.307 line:0%
Ah, that thing's harder
than $9 worth of jawbreakers

00:02:55.407 --> 00:02:57.710 line:7%
and straight as an arrow, man--

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.411 line:7%
pretty good birthday.

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:02.248 line:0%
JOE: It's day two, and
I'm looking at the blade.

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:08.087
And I'm not 100% on the
laminations on the san mai.

00:03:08.153 --> 00:03:10.723
So it's seeming to make
the best sense just

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:13.693
to scrap it and start over.

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:15.594
I'm going to use a big
old piece of leaf spring

00:03:15.661 --> 00:03:18.364
and see what I can do
a second time around.

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:21.801
Starting over with a
51/60 mono-steel blade,

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:23.536
time is really at a premium.

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:24.470
I may not finish.

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:30.443
 So it's the
start of day three.

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:33.079
I have to start putting a
lot of puzzle pieces together

00:03:33.179 --> 00:03:34.613
and do a lot of fabrication.

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:36.649
60's too hard.

00:03:36.715 --> 00:03:39.285
So I think I need to
temper this some more.

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:41.887
A little hard for my liking for
what it's going to be doing,

00:03:41.954 --> 00:03:44.290
so I'll soften it some more.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:47.026
I'm trying to make sure that
my blade gets up to temperature

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:48.527
and [inaudible]
stress, so that way

00:03:48.627 --> 00:03:52.698
I've got a nice flexible
yet strong blade.

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:56.168
If I don't get these blades
softened and more flexible,

00:03:56.235 --> 00:03:57.403
they're more likely to snap.

00:03:57.469 --> 00:03:59.272
Right now they're very brittle.

00:03:59.339 --> 00:04:03.042
If I heat up the very end
and keep heating up the end,

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:06.579
the heat will travel and draw
the temper all the way down.

00:04:06.645 --> 00:04:09.282
That's the best I
can do right now.

00:04:09.349 --> 00:04:12.185
I've got my dagger tempered,
so I can put my handle on.

00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:15.254
Then I'll slide my socket
on, weld that beast up,

00:04:15.354 --> 00:04:17.089
and we're ready to go.

00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:18.624
It fits right in there.

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:20.526
My blade is
completely assembled.

00:04:20.626 --> 00:04:23.395
It's not pretty, but
it would perform.

00:04:23.495 --> 00:04:26.599 line:7%
I think it's ready to roll, man.

00:04:26.665 --> 00:04:29.369 line:0%
JOE: So yesterday I forged
out the blade of my Bhuj.

00:04:29.469 --> 00:04:33.239 line:0%
I forged out the stiletto, and
I got around to heat-treating

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:35.408 line:7%
the Bhuj blade.

00:04:35.474 --> 00:04:38.577
Today I have to
heat-treat the stiletto.

00:04:38.678 --> 00:04:40.780
Heat-treating a
stiletto is going

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:43.549
to be a little tricky because
there's zero room for warpage.

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:45.484
So this thing needs to
be dead straight to be

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:46.819
able to fit in that handle.

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:48.687
If it's not, I mean, it
could hang up in there,

00:04:48.754 --> 00:04:52.392
or might not even come out, or
just rub against interior wall

00:04:52.492 --> 00:04:53.660
and dull the blade.

00:04:56.161 --> 00:04:58.864
So it's the moment of truth.

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:00.299
Yeah, it looks great.

00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:02.902
It looks perfectly straight.

00:05:02.969 --> 00:05:05.438
It's time to start chiseling
in the elephant head

00:05:05.538 --> 00:05:07.540
into the bolster now.

00:05:07.606 --> 00:05:09.608
I'm choosing to put
an elephant on my Bhuj

00:05:09.708 --> 00:05:11.911
because that was the
traditional creature

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:13.212
they would add onto it.

00:05:13.312 --> 00:05:16.381
And I'd really like
to honor the culture

00:05:16.448 --> 00:05:19.718
and these amazing smiths
for creating this.

00:05:19.785 --> 00:05:21.087
There we go.

00:05:21.187 --> 00:05:24.424
So the weapon as a whole I think
is becoming a beautiful piece.

00:05:37.603 --> 00:05:39.605
 Joe, Benton, welcome
back to the forge.

00:05:39.672 --> 00:05:41.840
You fellas have had four
days at your home forges

00:05:41.941 --> 00:05:45.144
to work on your Bhuj with
hidden stiletto blade.

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:46.612
Joe, how did it go?

00:05:46.713 --> 00:05:49.048 line:7%
 It went well.

00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:51.150 line:0%
My blade's made
out of leaf spring,

00:05:51.217 --> 00:05:56.054 line:0%
got a coil-spring stiletto, and
some etch design work on there.

00:05:56.121 --> 00:05:57.189 line:7%
 What about you, Benton?

00:05:57.289 --> 00:05:59.992 line:0%
 I feel like my
build went well.

00:06:00.093 --> 00:06:04.697 line:0%
My blade's out of 51/60,
and my stiletto is 10/84.

00:06:04.764 --> 00:06:07.133 line:0%
It was a tough build, but
I feel great about it.

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:09.802
 Well, gentlemen, only one of
you can be the "Forged in Fire"

00:06:09.869 --> 00:06:10.903
champion.

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:12.471
And to determine which
one of you it will be,

00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:14.106
it's time to test them.

00:06:14.173 --> 00:06:16.809
It will be a strength test, a
sharpness test, and, up first,

00:06:16.876 --> 00:06:17.809
the kill test.

00:06:17.876 --> 00:06:18.611
Doug.

00:06:21.247 --> 00:06:24.450
 Bladesmiths, welcome
to the kill test.

00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:27.386
Your Bhujes look beautiful,
but are they deadly?

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:29.421
Well, to find that out,
I will take your weapon

00:06:29.488 --> 00:06:34.526
and deliver killing
blows onto pig carcasses.

00:06:34.593 --> 00:06:35.794
Joe, you're up first.
Ready?

00:06:35.861 --> 00:06:36.328
 I'm ready.

00:06:36.429 --> 00:06:38.798
 Let's do this.

00:06:38.898 --> 00:06:40.098
JOE: My heart's racing.

00:06:40.165 --> 00:06:42.168
My knees are rattling.

00:06:42.268 --> 00:06:45.070
I just feel like
anything can happen.

00:06:45.137 --> 00:06:47.673
[rock music]

00:06:58.917 --> 00:06:59.619
 Nice.

00:07:17.403 --> 00:07:20.339
 Oh, man.

00:07:20.406 --> 00:07:21.207
[sigh]

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:25.278
 First up, this blade is sharp.

00:07:25.378 --> 00:07:28.480
The point is easy enough
to get into the carcass

00:07:28.547 --> 00:07:29.982
and smash on the way out.

00:07:30.049 --> 00:07:34.053
It's got a great feel
to it, nice stiletto.

00:07:34.153 --> 00:07:36.054
There's even a handle
that you put on this,

00:07:36.154 --> 00:07:39.357
so it gets a nice look to it.

00:07:39.458 --> 00:07:44.363
Overall, sir, this
Bhuj will kill.

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:45.698
 Thanks, Doug.

00:07:45.798 --> 00:07:48.567
 All right, Benton, are
you ready to ham it up?

00:07:48.634 --> 00:07:49.969
 Ready to rock and roll.

00:07:50.036 --> 00:07:51.937
 Let's do this.

00:07:52.004 --> 00:07:55.107
BENTON: Joe's Bhuj
performed incredibly.

00:07:55.174 --> 00:07:57.776
It split that pig in half.

00:07:57.876 --> 00:08:00.780
And now it's my turn,
and I'm terrified.

00:08:00.846 --> 00:08:03.483
I've never made this
style of weapon before.

00:08:03.583 --> 00:08:05.884
I've never been able to test
this kind of construction.

00:08:05.951 --> 00:08:09.254
I just don't know how
it's going to hold up.

00:08:09.354 --> 00:08:11.858
[rock music]

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:21.166
Oh, [bleep], man.

00:08:21.233 --> 00:08:22.401
 Sorry, man.

00:08:22.467 --> 00:08:25.538
 It's a big piece of shrapnel.

00:08:25.604 --> 00:08:27.139
 [bleep] damn it.

00:08:29.975 --> 00:08:33.112
 Well, Benton, one of the
things I like about this,

00:08:33.212 --> 00:08:34.747
you put on the leather.

00:08:34.813 --> 00:08:37.216
It gave me a very nice area
to hold onto, and it's ovoid.

00:08:37.282 --> 00:08:39.151
I can tell where the edge is.

00:08:39.218 --> 00:08:41.753
But the obvious happened.

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:43.855
It's a coarse-grain
structure here.

00:08:43.955 --> 00:08:46.592
 I should have normalized that
tang much better than I did.

00:08:46.659 --> 00:08:49.962
But when you're grinding
away long days in the shop

00:08:50.062 --> 00:08:51.764
during this challenge
and you're just

00:08:51.864 --> 00:08:54.367
focused on the finish line, it's
easy to overlook some things.

00:08:54.467 --> 00:08:57.303
And obviously I did.

00:08:57.403 --> 00:08:59.138
 Well, Ben, any warrior
knows that if you

00:08:59.205 --> 00:09:02.541
leave a piece of shrapnel that
big in a target, it's deadly.

00:09:02.608 --> 00:09:05.244
However, a warrior also
knows that his weapon

00:09:05.344 --> 00:09:06.612
needs to be strong.

00:09:06.712 --> 00:09:09.148
And your blade has suffered
a catastrophic failure

00:09:09.248 --> 00:09:11.050
in our very first test.

00:09:11.116 --> 00:09:14.586
And therefore, you cannot move
forward in this competition.

00:09:14.686 --> 00:09:17.355
Come on, brother--
did a great job, man.

00:09:17.456 --> 00:09:18.357
 [inaudible].

00:09:18.457 --> 00:09:19.925
I feel pretty bummed.

00:09:20.025 --> 00:09:22.929
But this challenge has been both
very difficult and invigorating

00:09:22.995 --> 00:09:24.063
at the same time.

00:09:24.163 --> 00:09:26.599
I've made things that
I've never made before,

00:09:26.665 --> 00:09:28.400
and I've overcome some
challenges that I've

00:09:28.467 --> 00:09:29.601
never had to face before.

00:09:29.668 --> 00:09:31.704
So overall, it was
a great experience.

00:09:35.274 --> 00:09:38.143
 Joe, your blade is
sharp, deadly, and strong.

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:40.245
And you are the new
"Forged in Fire" champion,

00:09:40.312 --> 00:09:43.081
and that's a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:09:43.148 --> 00:09:43.816
Good job.

00:09:43.883 --> 00:09:45.551
[applause]

00:09:45.618 --> 00:09:46.685
How do you feel right now?

00:09:46.752 --> 00:09:48.220
 It's a little surreal.

00:09:48.286 --> 00:09:50.288
I'm a "Forged in Fire" champion.

00:09:50.355 --> 00:09:51.590
I won.

00:09:51.657 --> 00:09:53.125
But you know, it
would've been nice to win

00:09:53.225 --> 00:09:54.559
after the three tests.

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:57.762
But this has been a
totally unique opportunity.

00:09:57.829 --> 00:10:00.866
It's really a big
affirmation of my abilities.

00:10:00.967 --> 00:10:02.668
It's amazing.

